x)$ is twice-differentiable, the tangent line to the graph exists for all real $x.$\n\nInflection points occur when a graph changes concavity. In order for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${h}^{″}(x)$ must switch signs. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={h}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, $h(x)$ has points of inflection at $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-114399/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "977a9b6e-744a-554b-92ee-0b6343041ecf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114399"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31219/selection/c404754c3a56e6275fb348852d227681c7496ded76f1b6144166f87b542b67e6" :answer/id #uuid "c4e389c4-06ed-5dc1-8e71-6f3093c74722" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31219/selection/5ffe894c68830d5babbad4a800990847c761cd499146f3799e17d4e0d80287d4" :answer/id #uuid "66acfaac-58a5-5185-a6d3-c3d0d2c80a85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-6$ and $x=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31219/selection/2972181eec371d69d372c80067546903c5c0bdf2fd3828215c312d0a2ffdee15" :answer/id #uuid "306164fa-4dd6-5c1a-a107-b6af8267d7b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-6$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31219/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "09b2ac1d-4454-5f3f-98b2-c98690ed692a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31219/selection/f35e47078a0b4e7924c5255f58c47330d5f103a7d52f7e2492c610f259ee6499" :answer/id #uuid "fdf65c2b-bc08-5529-b64a-1f85068785ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-6,\\,$ $x=-2,$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db